<Base title="Privacy and data handling" description="Illustrative Northstar policy for workspace records, exports, retention and deletion.">
<p class="eyebrow">Data handling</p><h1>Your workspace data, explained</h1><p class="lead">This fictional product policy defines the terms used by the demonstration. It is not a legal notice for a live service.</p><section><h2>What is stored</h2><p>Workspace member details, project tasks, client contact records and notes are the core record types. Do not enter actual personal or confidential data into this demo.</p><h2>Exports and deletion</h2><p>Both plans include CSV export for project and client records. The illustrative policy retains workspace records for 30 days after an account deletion request before removing them from active storage.</p><h2>Cancellation and access</h2><p>Subscription cancellation takes effect at the next renewal. Access continues until the current paid period ends. Cancellation and data deletion are separate actions.</p><h2>External documents</h2><p>Linked documents remain with their original provider and retain that provider’s access rules.</p><a href="/contact">Ask about data handling</a></section>
</Base>
